Z||000002||Tigger||10-18-2001||03:16 PM||||About week ago I saw an Olds Achieva(sp?) with a wrap aroundish spoiler that was made for those cars from the factory.<P>If it's possible to fit it on a Fiero it would look similar the spoiler on the Yellow Fiero MinnGreen posted but without the three vents.<P>Just an idea maybe worth looking into.  I'll try to dig up a picture.<P>Can't find a pitcher  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||10-18-2001||03:58 PM||||Great timing, I picked up a Euro Lumina spoiler yesterday in hopes that it might fit. Got it home and there's no way it will fit without major reconstruction. Don't waste your time with the Lumina spoiler. Anyone have a Lumina...want a spoiler?<P>OK, I took another look at it and it's not really that bad. The contour is close enough that it will bolt on pretty well. The tips need to be shortened about 6" of they could just be cut off square. The rear has a little too much curve. Note that in the pis it is sitting up on the studs.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lumina1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lumina2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lumina3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lumina4.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||10
